# Ye and Ghassemi (2018), specimen SW-S4.
#
# Units: m.
# Geometry (paper Table 1): length = 0.11870, diameter = 0.05051,
# fracture angle = 30 degrees, measured from the specimen's long/vertical axis to
# the fracture plane.
#
# FRACTURE-ANGLE CORRECTION -- branch fix/physics-verification-audit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This journal previously placed the plane at
#     z_high = 0.10207927   z_low = 0.01092073   (at x = +/- 0.025255)
# which is 28.990 degrees, not 30, AND centred it at z = 0.05650 instead of
# z = h/2 = 0.05935 (2.85 mm low).  The z-span 0.09115854 was bit-identical to the
# one in ye_ghassemi_2018_SWS3.jou, so the plane had been copied from SW-S3 (a
# genuine 29-degree specimen) and only shifted; the shift applied was 5.70 mm,
# exactly twice the 2.85 mm needed, so both the angle and the centring were wrong.
#
# 30 degrees is confirmed twice over.  Table 1 states it, and the paper's own
# Table 2 reproduces it through the identity
#     tan(theta) = (sigma'_n - sigma_3 + Pp) / tau        [sigma_3 = 30 MPa]
# which returns 0.5768-0.5801 (= tan 30 deg) at all eleven hold stages of SW-S4,
# loading and unloading.  See doc/theory/orca_czm_theory.md, Supplement.
#
# What the old 28.99-degree plane cost, at a given differential stress sigma_d:
#     tau      = sigma_d sin(th)cos(th) :  0.424024 vs 0.433013  -> 2.1% LOW
#     sigma'_n deviatoric part          :  0.235040 vs 0.250000  -> 6.1% LOW
#     fracture area pi D^2/(4 sin th)   :  4.1343e-3 vs 4.0075e-3 -> 3.2% LARGE
# The SW-S4 decks always reduced at 30 degrees (bulk_sin_theta = 0.5), so the mesh
# was the outlier, not the decks.
#
# Corrected plane, centred at z = h/2 = 0.05935, at x = +/- r = 0.025255:
#     z = h/2 +/- r cot(30 deg) = 0.05935 +/- 0.0437429431
#     z_high = 0.1030929431      z_low = 0.0156070569
#
# AFTER REGENERATING, the injection/production source coordinates in every SW-S4
# deck must move onto the new plane (boreholes sit 6 mm inside the sidewall, i.e.
# at x = +/- 0.019255):
#     source_in   coord = '-0.019255 0 0.025999362'    (was 0.021745)
#     source_out  coord = ' 0.019255 0 0.092700638'    (was 0.091255)
# `use_closest_node = true` will otherwise snap silently to a node several mm away
# along the plane.  Run meshes/apply_30deg_source_coords.py; see
# meshes/README_fracture_angle.md.
#
# Expected fracture_interface area after the split: 4.0075e-3 m^2.
# NOTE axial_pres_final was gated on the old 28.99-degree geometry and will need a
# ~2% trim; re-gate it with a short run before submitting production jobs.

reset
create Cylinder height 0.1187 radius 0.025255
move Volume 1  z 0.05935 include_merged 
 
create vertex location 0.025255 0.025255 0.1030929431
create vertex location 0.025255 -0.025255 0.1030929431
create vertex location -0.025255 -0.025255 0.0156070569
webcut volume 1 with plane vertex 3 vertex 4 vertex 5
delete vertex 3 4 5
webcut volume all with plane xplane imprint merge 
webcut volume all with plane yplane imprint merge 
imprint all
merge all

vol all size auto factor 1   # 5 -> ye_ghassemi_2018_SWS4_size_5.e ; 3 -> _size_3.e
volume all scheme polyhedron 
mesh volume all

block 1 add volume 2 4 8 6 
block 1 name "top_block"

block 2 add volume 1 3 5 7
block 2 name "bottom_block"

# block 1 element type HEX27
# block 2 element type HEX27

nodeset 1 add surface 36 56 63 42  
nodeset 1 name "top_nodeset"
nodeset 2 add surface 28 30 50 48  
nodeset 2 name "bottom_nodeset"
nodeset 3 add surface 33 43 61 51 25 35 57 47  
nodeset 3 name "sides_nodeset"
nodeset 4 add surface 26 46 53 32 
nodeset 4 name "fracture_interface"
nodeset 5 add vertex 27 34 41 48
nodeset 5 name "no_disp_x"
nodeset 6 add vertex 10 11 18 19
nodeset 6 name"no_disp_y"
